From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Yocto RK3399 <you@example.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Feb 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] linuxcnc: use system tools and ensure Tcl can find Linuxcnc

On the target image, /usr/bin/linuxcnc currently contains hardcoded
paths to the Yocto hosttools directory, e.g.:

  PIDOF="/home/xuning/yocto-rk3399/build/tmp/hosttools/pidof -x"
  GREP=/home/xuning/yocto-rk3399/build/tmp/hosttools/grep

Those paths only exist on the build host, not on the target system,
so running linuxcnc fails with errors such as:

  /usr/bin/linuxcnc: line 339: /home/.../hosttools/grep: No such file or directory

The correct behaviour is to use the target's own pidof/ps/awk/grep/ipcs/kill
found in $PATH.

In addition, the Tcl helper script hallib/check_config.tcl calls:

  package require Linuxcnc

but does not ensure that the Linuxcnc Tcl package directory is present
on Tcl's auto_path, which can cause "can't find package Linuxcnc" at
runtime on Yocto systems.

This patch fixes both issues:

* linuxcnc.in: drop hardcoded hosttools paths and use plain command
  names, preserving the upstream "-x" argument for pidof.
* lib/hallib/check_config.tcl: prepend /usr/lib/tcltk/linuxcnc to
  auto_path before "package require Linuxcnc".

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [Yocto-specific path handling]

Signed-off-by: Yocto RK3399 <you@example.com>

---
 scripts/linuxcnc.in           | 10 +++++-----
 lib/hallib/check_config.tcl   |  3 +++
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/linuxcnc.in b/scripts/linuxcnc.in
index 000000000000..111111111111 100755
--- a/scripts/linuxcnc.in
+++ b/scripts/linuxcnc.in
@@ -39,12 +39,12 @@
 prefix=@prefix@
 exec_prefix=@exec_prefix@
 
-PIDOF="@PIDOF@ -x"
-PS=@PS@
-AWK=@AWK@
-GREP=@GREP@
-IPCS=@IPCS@
-KILL=@KILL@
+# Use the target system binaries instead of build-host tools
+PIDOF="pidof -x"
+PS=ps
+AWK=awk
+GREP=grep
+IPCS=ipcs
+KILL=kill
 
 LINUXCNC_HOME=@EMC2_HOME@; export LINUXCNC_HOME
 
diff --git a/lib/hallib/check_config.tcl b/lib/hallib/check_config.tcl
index 222222222222..333333333333 100755
--- a/lib/hallib/check_config.tcl
+++ b/lib/hallib/check_config.tcl
@@ -186,6 +186,9 @@ proc warn_for_multiple_ini_values {} {
 } ;# warn_for_multiple_ini_values
 
 #----------------------------------------------------------------------
 # begin
+# Ensure the Linuxcnc Tcl package is visible
+lappend auto_path /usr/lib/tcltk/linuxcnc
+
 package require Linuxcnc ;# parse_ini
 
 set ::progname [file rootname [file tail [info script]]]
